WEBVTT

00:02.544 --> 00:03.753
You know,

00:03.837 --> 00:07.507
they say that torii gates
are the front door of a god's home.

00:08.049 --> 00:11.970
Imagine you get home after a mission

00:12.053 --> 00:14.222
and find your front door in shambles.

00:14.305 --> 00:15.890
How sad would that be?

00:15.974 --> 00:19.185
But you were busy eating <i>katsudon.</i>

00:19.269 --> 00:21.312
Because I was finishing your leftovers.

00:25.316 --> 00:26.693
Hello?

00:26.776 --> 00:28.820
<i>Hey. How's it going, Shishiba?</i>

00:30.321 --> 00:33.074
<i>Nagumo. Are you eating something?</i>

00:33.616 --> 00:35.493
I'm at work. It's my break.

00:35.577 --> 00:37.704
<i>You've got a side-gig?</i>

00:38.204 --> 00:40.498
Did you see the list the inmates had?

00:41.207 --> 00:43.168
Check out the last page.

00:44.335 --> 00:45.670
One moment.

00:49.466 --> 00:51.259
So this was Slur's plan all along...

00:51.342 --> 00:52.385
DUMP
SAW

00:52.469 --> 00:55.805
He meant to have the inmates
kill each other in the end.

00:55.889 --> 00:56.765
MINIMALIST

00:57.348 --> 01:00.977
Now that's twisted...
And practical, I suppose.

01:01.561 --> 01:03.188
Actually,

01:03.730 --> 01:06.232
I think they were meant to drag it out.

01:06.316 --> 01:08.401
<i>What are you saying?</i>

01:08.985 --> 01:11.321
This is turning out to be a real pain.

01:11.404 --> 01:12.906
MIKAN

02:44.956 --> 02:47.208
ROUND AND ROUND THE TOWER

02:47.292 --> 02:48.418
What's that?

02:59.470 --> 03:00.471
Incredible...

03:01.055 --> 03:03.349
This is the longest connection I've had!

03:03.933 --> 03:05.351
You're the first...

03:06.394 --> 03:07.604
Will you...

03:08.646 --> 03:11.441
listen to what I have to say?

03:12.525 --> 03:13.568
Sorry.

03:16.613 --> 03:19.407
I don't have the time
to listen to you blabber.

03:25.622 --> 03:26.831
What a cold-blooded man.

03:30.835 --> 03:31.836
Got it wound up.

03:37.717 --> 03:38.718
Hey.

03:39.469 --> 03:42.722
Do you remember the first time
you connected with the world?

03:42.805 --> 03:45.225
What are you talking about?

03:45.975 --> 03:49.687
You know, the first time you felt like
you weren't alone in this world.

03:50.855 --> 03:52.982
I remember it clearly.

03:55.485 --> 03:57.987
<i>I didn't get along well
with the other kids.</i>

03:58.780 --> 04:00.240
I got it!

04:01.032 --> 04:02.200
You suck.

04:06.871 --> 04:07.789
I'm home.

04:09.415 --> 04:11.209
<i>My mom didn't care about me.</i>

04:11.793 --> 04:13.962
<i>We barely ever talked to each other.</i>

04:14.045 --> 04:15.463
<i>I don't even remember her voice.</i>

04:17.298 --> 04:18.591
<i>But...</i>

04:18.675 --> 04:20.468
Hey, now, Apart!

04:20.551 --> 04:23.513
What's the matter?
You're all down in the dumps.

04:23.596 --> 04:25.473
Did you eat a pickle by accident?

04:26.182 --> 04:28.309
<i>My dad was the only one
who was kind to me.</i>

04:28.935 --> 04:31.646
<i>He was always busy with work,
so I didn't see him much,</i>

04:32.355 --> 04:34.023
<i>but I liked my dad.</i>

04:35.149 --> 04:36.484
Listen to me, Apart.

04:37.068 --> 04:40.113
With people,
it's what's on the inside that matters.

04:40.196 --> 04:43.992
Just be honest and kind to your friends.

04:44.075 --> 04:46.703
I'm sure everyone will realize
how great you are.

04:47.328 --> 04:49.622
You're a good kid, Apart.

04:49.706 --> 04:51.958
But first, you need some practice!

04:52.041 --> 04:54.377
Here. I got you something.

04:55.003 --> 04:56.713
Hi, Apart!

04:56.796 --> 04:58.923
Will you be my friend?

05:06.973 --> 05:08.057
Um...

05:08.641 --> 05:10.143
Can I play with...

05:10.727 --> 05:12.186
Who the heck are you?

05:12.270 --> 05:13.146
What a creep.

05:23.781 --> 05:25.241
I don't get it.

05:26.075 --> 05:28.494
Why won't they play with me?

05:36.252 --> 05:37.670
Who the heck are you?

06:30.556 --> 06:32.767
Dad! Welcome home.

06:33.309 --> 06:36.062
Dad, guess what! I...

06:39.816 --> 06:41.984
I'm sorry, Apart.

06:43.194 --> 06:44.278
It's gonna be okay.

06:44.779 --> 06:47.698
Tomorrow, we'll go to the doctor together.

06:53.037 --> 06:56.249
There's nothing wrong with him.
He's the picture of health.

06:56.332 --> 06:58.876
We didn't find any tumors or anything.

06:59.460 --> 07:00.920
Nothing... wrong...?

07:01.712 --> 07:03.005
That can't be true.

07:04.132 --> 07:05.174
So, what?

07:05.675 --> 07:07.051
Are you telling me

07:07.635 --> 07:09.637
that there's nothing wrong with my son,

07:09.720 --> 07:12.432
that he just tore an animal apart
because he wanted to?

07:13.516 --> 07:14.350
Well, uh...

07:16.477 --> 07:17.937
Are you insinuating

07:18.020 --> 07:20.982
that he was born a monster?!

07:21.065 --> 07:22.150
Dad!

07:22.233 --> 07:23.151
Get away from me!

07:23.734 --> 07:24.694
You creep me out.

07:25.319 --> 07:26.612
What the hell are you?

07:42.837 --> 07:43.713
I'm...

07:44.297 --> 07:46.466
I'm not a monster!

07:55.183 --> 07:56.476
Wow...

07:57.059 --> 08:00.980
Look, Dad!
Your brain looks just like mine!

08:01.772 --> 08:06.110
We're just the same on the inside!

08:08.905 --> 08:10.031
Thank goodness.

08:11.073 --> 08:12.617
I'm...

08:13.284 --> 08:15.119
connected with everyone after all.

08:17.788 --> 08:20.041
That was the first time I ever thought,

08:20.625 --> 08:22.835
"Oh, I'm not alone."

08:23.836 --> 08:25.963
"I'm human, just like everyone else."

08:27.507 --> 08:31.052
This is how I confirm
my connection with others.

08:31.844 --> 08:34.514
So if you don't mind,
I'd like to see inside you too.

08:34.597 --> 08:36.057
You're wrong.

08:37.558 --> 08:41.062
When you kill someone, all you're doing
is severing that connection.

08:42.188 --> 08:44.023
You need to stop hurting people.

08:46.234 --> 08:49.320
How dare you.
You can't dismiss my way of life.

08:49.820 --> 08:53.115
I can't believe how inconsiderate you are.

09:00.873 --> 09:02.542
Hey, is the tower tipping over?

09:03.167 --> 09:05.294
Hey, we're tipping over!

09:06.546 --> 09:07.880
Wow!

09:07.964 --> 09:09.715
It's like a slide!

09:10.341 --> 09:11.592
That does it.

09:12.426 --> 09:14.720
After I kill you and take you apart,

09:14.804 --> 09:16.973
I'll leave your body parts unorganized.

09:18.224 --> 09:21.477
You don't have the right
to talk about human connection.

09:24.564 --> 09:26.524
This ends here.

09:33.447 --> 09:34.407
What?

09:34.490 --> 09:36.409
Wait a second...

09:36.492 --> 09:39.287
Does the tower look like it's leaning?

09:39.829 --> 09:41.664
That can't be good, right?

09:43.249 --> 09:45.418
This is not good, Taro!

09:49.046 --> 09:50.131
<i>This is bad.</i>

09:52.133 --> 09:53.426
I'm so excited.

09:54.010 --> 09:56.679
I'll get to connect with all these people!

09:56.762 --> 09:59.765
I bet my dad would be so proud
if he found out about this.

10:05.187 --> 10:07.064
<i>Power lines...</i>

10:13.404 --> 10:15.740
<i>Good thing I'm heavy.</i>

10:22.038 --> 10:23.372
It stopped...

10:24.081 --> 10:26.083
Should we head down while we can?

10:26.167 --> 10:27.752
My head is spinning.

10:28.419 --> 10:30.796
I was in the middle of talking.

10:30.880 --> 10:32.715
It's rude to walk away.

10:34.842 --> 10:37.678
Time for you to show me
what's on the inside.

10:38.304 --> 10:39.305
<i>What do I do?</i>

10:41.474 --> 10:42.433
<i>What's that?</i>

11:06.874 --> 11:08.417
What is going on?!

11:08.501 --> 11:11.504
It looked like it was going to fall down,
but did it stop?

11:11.587 --> 11:15.508
It did stop, but...
it looks kind of weird now.

11:16.092 --> 11:17.968
Did Taro do that?!

11:19.303 --> 11:20.513
Why?

11:20.596 --> 11:23.474
<i>That threatening aura... Could it be?</i>

11:27.061 --> 11:29.355
Hey, Gramps!
You done in the bathroom already?

11:31.148 --> 11:34.318
Did you hear that huge noise just now?

11:34.819 --> 11:36.904
Anyway, this is my chance.

11:36.987 --> 11:39.156
I'll make him feel my weight.

11:47.456 --> 11:48.290
<i>So heavy!</i>

12:11.105 --> 12:12.356
Damn you!

12:12.440 --> 12:16.777
Why won't you let me connect with you?!

12:27.830 --> 12:29.623
Why am I the only one...

12:30.332 --> 12:34.086
I'm human, just like everyone else!

12:34.670 --> 12:35.921
So why?!

12:37.548 --> 12:41.218
<i>Why is it so hard for me
to live in this world?!</i>

12:51.687 --> 12:54.732
You have the choice
to change how you live your life.

12:54.815 --> 12:56.192
So...

12:58.027 --> 12:59.987
I won't let go of this string.

13:27.181 --> 13:28.098
Cool!

13:30.351 --> 13:31.268
SKY TOWER
STAMP RALLY

13:31.352 --> 13:32.269
There we go.

13:33.437 --> 13:35.272
Mission accomplished.

13:35.856 --> 13:37.107
Thanks!

13:41.153 --> 13:42.238
<i>What a hassle.</i>

13:42.780 --> 13:45.741
<i>All that just so we can talk.</i>

13:47.159 --> 13:50.079
MIYA CLINIC
PHYSICAL THERAPY - ACUPUNCTURE

13:50.621 --> 13:53.207
Aw, the tea's all gone.

13:54.416 --> 13:55.918
Hey, Lu!

13:56.001 --> 13:57.545
Get your leg out of my space!

13:58.128 --> 14:01.674
Granny, do you mind
if I make another pot of tea?

14:01.757 --> 14:02.633
Do what you want.

14:03.133 --> 14:05.386
<i>What? Where am I?</i>

14:05.928 --> 14:09.223
<i>I was fighting Sakamoto at the tower
just a minute ago, wasn't I?</i>

14:09.848 --> 14:11.559
<i>Why is this table warm?</i>

14:12.142 --> 14:12.977
<i>What is this?</i>

14:13.769 --> 14:16.188
THE HIT MAN POST
UNSOLVED CASE FROM 18 YEARS AGO

14:16.939 --> 14:18.816
<i>Who are all these people?</i>

14:22.152 --> 14:24.154
Hey. You're awake, huh?

14:25.573 --> 14:27.491
Pretending to sleep won't work on me.

14:29.910 --> 14:31.495
What do you want?

14:31.579 --> 14:33.914
Are you with that deer guy too?

14:34.498 --> 14:36.458
You just want to use me, don't you?

14:37.459 --> 14:38.502
Well, I won't let you.

14:38.586 --> 14:40.713
I don't take orders from anyone!

14:40.796 --> 14:42.047
Use you?

14:42.548 --> 14:45.593
No, no, it's nothing like that.

14:46.302 --> 14:50.681
We just want you
to help us with something.

14:52.224 --> 14:53.559
What do you mean?

14:54.643 --> 14:58.230
Wait, why haven't you killed me?

14:59.315 --> 15:01.525
You can thank Mr. Sakamoto for that!

15:02.192 --> 15:03.360
Come, sit down.

15:03.861 --> 15:06.280
We have no grudge with you.

15:08.032 --> 15:12.202
We just want some information
on the person who hired you.

15:12.286 --> 15:15.956
Yeah! You're the only one we can count on.

15:16.040 --> 15:19.084
I'll give you this <i>mikan</i> if you help us.
What do you say?

15:20.002 --> 15:22.254
<i>The only one... they can count on...?</i>

15:22.922 --> 15:27.343
Did you not think
I would attack you once I woke up?

15:27.927 --> 15:28.886
You might've.

15:29.386 --> 15:30.638
But I had a hunch

15:31.138 --> 15:34.767
that you'd change your mind,
so we took the chance.

15:37.061 --> 15:38.854
Besides, if you did try something,

15:39.438 --> 15:42.483
I could just slam you
into Sky Tower again.

15:45.110 --> 15:48.864
Gotta say, I'm impressed
you survived getting beat up by Taro.

15:48.948 --> 15:51.784
I know you're the enemy,
but I still feel sorry for you.

15:51.867 --> 15:55.996
If Mr. Sakamoto hadn't held back,
you'd be six feet under right now.

15:56.080 --> 15:57.539
You should count yourself lucky.

15:58.415 --> 16:01.752
<i>They're talking to me
like I'm a normal person...</i>

16:05.297 --> 16:06.966
<i>What a bunch of weirdos.</i>

16:09.343 --> 16:12.054
What do you want me to tell you?

16:12.137 --> 16:14.515
All right! Thanks!

16:17.643 --> 16:21.271
The guy we met was part human,
part machine, and looked like a deer.

16:21.814 --> 16:23.524
I don't know who Slur is.

16:23.607 --> 16:26.318
Part human, part machine,
and looks like a deer?

16:27.236 --> 16:28.487
<i>So it's him.</i>

16:28.570 --> 16:30.781
You know who that is, Mr. Sakamoto?

16:30.864 --> 16:31.824
Yes.

16:32.324 --> 16:34.118
So? Where did you meet with him?

16:34.910 --> 16:37.788
I went to the hotel he's staying at once.

16:39.581 --> 16:43.168
<i>Things got heated and I tore him apart.</i>

16:43.252 --> 16:44.169
<i>But after that...</i>

16:44.920 --> 16:48.465
<i>I left one of my strings in there
and listened in for a while.</i>

16:49.466 --> 16:52.678
<i>This is just what we need
to get the jump on the JAA.</i>

16:53.429 --> 16:56.390
<i>Let them keep wreaking havoc.</i>

16:56.473 --> 17:01.270
Then we move on to phase two
according to plan?

17:01.854 --> 17:03.647
<i>Yes. We shall.</i>

17:04.356 --> 17:07.484
While The Order
is distracted by the inmates,

17:08.444 --> 17:10.654
we'll destroy their base of operations.

17:12.364 --> 17:16.910
They're planning to wipe out the JAA
in one swoop while it's shorthanded.

17:17.745 --> 17:20.956
I don't think you guys
should get too involved.

17:21.582 --> 17:23.667
Not that I know much about it all.

17:27.755 --> 17:32.176
<i>The Japanese Association of Assassins,
JAA for short.</i>

17:32.718 --> 17:34.678
<i>Boasting over 1,000 members,</i>

17:34.762 --> 17:38.057
<i>nearly 400 of whom
are professional hit men.</i>

17:38.140 --> 17:41.393
<i>It is the largest assassin organization
in Japan.</i>

17:45.397 --> 17:47.316
KILL

17:47.399 --> 17:48.317
Next!

17:52.029 --> 17:55.699
The recoil is so strong, it keeps jamming.

17:56.617 --> 17:58.827
The slide isn't going all the way back.

17:58.911 --> 18:01.455
This'll be useless in combat
unless we fix it.

18:02.414 --> 18:05.709
<i>Here, at the JAA Kanto branch,</i>

18:05.793 --> 18:11.048
<i>they provide mission support to assassins,
including management, mediation, and more.</i>

18:13.217 --> 18:16.595
Thank you for calling the JAA.
Would you like to request a mission?

18:16.678 --> 18:18.931
Will this be a murder or an accident?

18:19.014 --> 18:20.849
A murder. Yes, of course.

18:20.933 --> 18:25.562
<i>In addition, they make repairs
to public areas damaged during missions</i>

18:25.646 --> 18:29.858
<i>as well as the development
and manufacturing of new weapons.</i>

18:29.942 --> 18:33.779
<i>In other words,
they are the beating heart of the JAA.</i>

18:33.862 --> 18:35.739
<i>And today, at this very location,</i>

18:35.823 --> 18:39.827
<i>an incident unprecedented in JAA history
is about to take place.</i>

18:41.495 --> 18:43.372
Wow, big place.

18:43.455 --> 18:45.499
This is the JAA?

18:45.582 --> 18:46.542
Yes.

18:46.625 --> 18:48.127
Though it's not the headquarters.

18:48.836 --> 18:50.838
I knew they were loaded.

18:51.713 --> 18:53.715
Where should I park the bike?

18:53.799 --> 18:57.386
Go in right here. I think they had
bicycle parking in the back.

18:59.471 --> 19:02.516
Excuse me.
May I ask what your business here is?

19:03.100 --> 19:04.476
To enter this building,

19:04.560 --> 19:08.147
you'll either need a visitor's pass
or an employee ID.

19:08.230 --> 19:10.566
Well, actually...

19:10.649 --> 19:13.193
we're not JAA assassins.

19:13.277 --> 19:14.945
I see.

19:15.737 --> 19:18.073
Then I'll have to assume you're intruders.

19:18.157 --> 19:22.244
Following JAA regulations,
you will now be eliminated.

19:23.120 --> 19:26.081
Hey, Boss,
don't you have your JAA license?

19:26.165 --> 19:29.585
I didn't like how my photo turned out,
so I threw it away.

19:29.668 --> 19:32.588
I feel you.
They always take those pictures

19:32.671 --> 19:34.590
without any warning, don't they?

19:38.010 --> 19:39.178
Wha...

19:41.180 --> 19:44.099
I haven't stepped foot in here in ages.

19:44.183 --> 19:45.684
I feel a bit nervous.

19:46.435 --> 19:48.896
It's kind of like
going back to school after holidays.

19:48.979 --> 19:50.105
SLUR

19:50.189 --> 19:51.356
That jittery feeling.

19:51.440 --> 19:54.067
Oh, I get that.

19:54.151 --> 19:57.613
Like seeing your classmates
the day after you get a haircut.

19:58.238 --> 19:59.281
Exactly.

19:59.364 --> 20:01.241
You get nervous too, huh, Boss?

20:01.325 --> 20:04.661
The reason your performance suffers
when you're nervous is because

20:04.745 --> 20:09.750
you become too self-conscious
about your normal movements.

20:09.833 --> 20:12.419
You got that from one of your books again,
didn't you?

20:14.004 --> 20:17.049
So let's try to relax, Gaku.

20:17.132 --> 20:19.968
Don't tell <i>me</i> that.
You're the one who's nervous.

20:22.221 --> 20:24.723
One step closer to noble justice.

20:25.599 --> 20:28.101
Destroying the JAA?

20:28.185 --> 20:31.730
That Slur is definitely crazy, huh?

20:31.813 --> 20:33.774
What should we do, Mr. Sakamoto?

20:36.109 --> 20:38.779
For now, let's head to the JAA.

20:38.862 --> 20:39.863
What?

22:12.539 --> 22:13.749
There we go.

22:14.458 --> 22:17.085
What do you do on your days off, Shin?

22:17.169 --> 22:21.381
Me? Well, recently I've been
hanging out with Heisuke.

22:21.465 --> 22:22.341
Check it out.

22:23.050 --> 22:26.720
The other day, we did airsoft
and then went to a hot spring.

22:26.803 --> 22:29.097
Wow, you two are close!

22:29.181 --> 22:31.224
What about you?

22:32.726 --> 22:36.021
Actually, I hung out with Heisuke too.
We went to the arcade.

22:36.605 --> 22:40.025
See? There was this new zombie game
that I wanted to play.

22:40.108 --> 22:42.861
He looks so scared!

22:43.987 --> 22:46.239
Mr. Sakamoto! Good morning!

22:46.323 --> 22:49.618
Mr. Sakamoto,
what have you been doing on your days off?

22:52.829 --> 22:55.457
Yesterday, we had hot pot with Heisuke.

22:55.540 --> 22:56.374
Huh?!

22:56.458 --> 22:57.375
What?

22:57.459 --> 22:59.211
Nothing, it's just...

22:59.294 --> 23:02.422
We've been spending time with Heisuke
on our days off too.

23:02.506 --> 23:05.008
Everyone's hanging out with Heisuke!

23:05.092 --> 23:08.011
Well, he's always free, so...

23:11.640 --> 23:14.434
Here goes the roller coaster!

23:14.518 --> 23:17.312
- Whoosh!
- This is so fun!

23:17.395 --> 23:21.525
- Going up! Going down! Loop-the-loop!
- How nice, Hana!

23:23.652 --> 23:24.861
He's so popular!

23:24.945 --> 23:25.946
Subtitle translation by: Joshua Kizuki
